[C] GAUSSIAN BUNDLE:  mu = nu(dU') x N(0, sigma^2(U'))  =>  c(U') = sigma^2(U')
==============================================================================
  C1 continuous sigma^2 in [1.000000, 1.573505]:
     sup c = 1.5735053528   ess-sup c = 1.5735053528   ratio = 1.000000000000
  C2 spike at ONE grid point (nu-mass 1.0e-04):  sup = 1000.0   ess-sup = 1.5735053528   ratio = 635.5
     => D3-full holds with lambda_f = 0.635524 while D2 needs 1.0e-03
     => the two definitions DO differ, but only on a nu-null set; and for a Gibbs
        specification U' -> c(U') is a sup of continuous functions (lsc) while the
        coarse wavefunction has full support, which forces ess-sup = sup
  C3 two-valued sigma^2 (mass 1-p at 1, mass p=0.10 at 1+K, K=1e+03):
     lambda_weak = 1/E_nu[sigma^2] = 9.900990e-03   lambda_full = 1/sup sigma^2 = 9.990010e-04
     ratio lambda_weak/lambda_full = 9.9109   (a big 'gain' -- and still useless:)
     D3-weak does NOT control F = 1_A(U')*xi :  E_nu[Var]/E|grad_perp|^2 = 1+K = 1001
     => D3-weak strictly weaker than D3-full, and NOT sufficient for the assembly

